From: Benjamin Larsson <benjamin.larsson@genexis.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: add WED Kconfig option and Makefile rules

Add CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_SOC_WED tristate and wire up the build rules
for airoha_wed.c, airoha_wed_debugfs.c, and airoha_wed_ops.c.

airoha_wed_ops.o is built as a standalone object (not part of airoha-eth)
so that it is available before any WiFi driver loads, mirroring the
structure of drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed_ops.c.

Add ccflags-y to include the MediaTek ethernet driver directory so that
airoha_wed.h can include the private mtk_wed_regs.h header using a simple
filename rather than a relative path.

Signed-off-by: Benjamin Larsson <benjamin.larsson@genexis.eu>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/Kconfig  | 11 +++++++++++
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/Makefile |  4 ++++
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/Kconfig
@@ -31,4 +31,15 @@
 	help
 	  Enable Aiorha flowtable statistic counters.
 
+config NET_AIROHA_SOC_WED
+	tristate "Airoha EN7523 WED support"
+	depends on NET_AIROHA
+	help
+	  Enable WiFi Ethernet Datapath (WED) hardware offload for the
+	  EN7523 SoC.  When enabled, mt76 WiFi drivers can offload
+	  WiFi-to-Ethernet TX through the WED engine rather than taking
+	  the slow path through the CPU.
+
+	  If unsure, say M.
+
 endif #NET_VENDOR_AIROHA
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/Makefile
@@ -7,3 +7,7 @@
 airoha-eth-y := airoha_eth.o airoha_ppe.o
 airoha-eth-$(CONFIG_DEBUG_FS) += airoha_ppe_debugfs.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_NPU) += airoha_npu.o
+
+ccflags-y += -I$(srctree)/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek
+obj-$(CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_SOC_WED) += airoha_wed_ops.o
+airoha-eth-$(CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_SOC_WED) += airoha_wed.o airoha_wed_debugfs.o
